    rdfs:label "NICE reference case for health effects (PMG36, 2022)"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000114 obo:IAO_0000122 ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A reference case profile setting the methods NICE required for measuring, valuing and discounting health effects in its 2022 manual (PMG36), before the adoption of the EQ-5D-5L value set."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "Superseded for new topics by PMG51 (27 August 2026). Topics started before that date keep these rules, so the profile stays valid for them (PMG51 1.17, 1.18)."@en,
        "Under PMG36, utilities came from the EQ-5D-3L UK value set (Dolan 1997); EQ-5D-5L responses were mapped to it with the NICE DSU mapping (Hernández Alava et al. 2017) using the EEPRU dataset (Hernández Alava et al. 2023), and the EQ-5D-5L value set for England (Devlin et al. 2018) was not recommended (old PMG36 4.3.16, as quoted in PMG51). The value set rules do not apply to EQ-5D-Y data."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000117 <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9502-4678>,
        <https://orcid.org/0009-0006-0231-3731> ;
    obo:IAO_0000118 "NICE reference case for health effects (2022)"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000119 "NICE 2022 (PMG36)" ;
    dcterms:issued "2022-01-31" ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "NICE PMG36 reference case"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/oheo> ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/oheo/reference-case-shapes#NICE_PMG36_2022> .

oheo:0000392 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        oheo:0000327 ;
    rdfs:label "Second Panel reference case for health effects"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000114 obo:IAO_0000125 ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A reference case profile setting the methods the Second Panel on Cost-Effectiveness in Health and Medicine recommends for cost-effectiveness analyses in the United States."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "Facts carried over from 0.1.0 and not re-checked for this release."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000117 <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9502-4678>,
        <https://orcid.org/0009-0006-0231-3731> ;
    obo:IAO_0000119 "Sanders et al. 2016" ;
    dcterms:issued "2016" ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "Second Panel reference case"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/oheo> ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/oheo/reference-case-shapes#SecondPanel_2016> .

oheo:0000393 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        oheo:0000327 ;
    rdfs:label "CDA-AMC reference case for health effects"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000114 obo:IAO_0000125 ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A reference case profile setting the methods Canada's Drug Agency (CDA-AMC, formerly CADTH) requires for measuring, valuing and discounting health effects in economic evaluations."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "Carer health effects are included where they are meaningful; spillovers beyond patients and informal carers go in non-reference-case analyses. Sensitivity analyses at 0% and 3%."@en,
        "Facts carried over from 0.1.0 and not re-checked for this release."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000117 <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9502-4678>,
        <https://orcid.org/0009-0006-0231-3731> ;
    obo:IAO_0000119 "CADTH 2017 (Guidelines for the Economic Evaluation of Health Technologies: Canada, 4th edition)" ;
    dcterms:issued "2017" ;
    oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym "CADTH reference case"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/oheo> ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/oheo/reference-case-shapes#CDA_AMC_2017> .

oheo:0000394 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        oheo:0000327 ;
    rdfs:label "PBAC base case for health effects"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000114 obo:IAO_0000125 ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A reference case profile setting the methods the Pharmaceutical Benefits Advisory Committee (Australia) requires for measuring, valuing and discounting health effects in submissions."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "Facts carried over from 0.1.0 and not re-checked for this release."@en,
        "QALYs apply where a cost-utility analysis is presented, which PBAC prefers when life is extended or quality of life improves. Sensitivity analyses at 3.5% and 0%; PBAC consulted on its discount rate in 2022."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000117 <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9502-4678>,
        <https://orcid.org/0009-0006-0231-3731> ;
    obo:IAO_0000119 "PBAC 2016 (Guidelines for preparing submissions to the PBAC, version 5.0); PBAC reviewed its base discount rate in July 2022, so the current rate needs checking" ;
    dcterms:issued "2016" ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/oheo> ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/oheo/reference-case-shapes#PBAC_2016> .

oheo:0000395 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        oheo:0000327 ;
    rdfs:label "IQWiG approach to health effects in economic evaluation"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000114 obo:IAO_0000125 ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A reference case profile setting the methods the Institute for Quality and Efficiency in Health Care (Germany) uses for health effects in its assessments of the relation of benefits to costs."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "Facts carried over from 0.1.0 and not re-checked for this release."@en,
        "The base case perspective is that of the community of people insured by statutory health insurance. Sensitivity analyses at 0%, 5%, 7% and 10%."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000117 <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9502-4678>,
        <https://orcid.org/0009-0006-0231-3731> ;
    obo:IAO_0000119 "IQWiG General Methods (the 0.1.0 draft cited version 6.1, 2022; version 7.0, 2023, is current and has not been checked)" ;
    dcterms:issued "2022" ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/oheo> ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/oheo/reference-case-shapes#IQWiG_2022> .

oheo:0000396 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        oheo:0000327 ;
    rdfs:label "ICER reference case for health effects"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000114 obo:IAO_0000122 ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A reference case profile setting the methods the Institute for Clinical and Economic Review (United States) uses for measuring, valuing and discounting health effects."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "Checked by reviewer B on 16 October 2026 against ICER's reference case document: 3% for costs and outcomes; EQ-5D-5L preferred if available, with no measure required. QALYs are reported with the equal value of life-years gained."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000117 <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9502-4678>,
